t**\\\\n\\\\nThis section, based on Supervisor Tarkin's detailed plan, covers the site's interactive elements and fulfills the critical 'no-code' update requirement.\\\\n\\\\n*   **Contact Form:** A standard contact form with client-side validation will provide a simple way for users to send messages, which will be submitted to a secure backend endpoint.\\\\n*   **News Feed:** The public news feed will be dynamically populated by fetching a simple `feed.json` file from S3, ensuring fast load times and easy updates.\\\\n*   **'No-Code' News Update System:** This is the cornerstone of the user-friendly management experience. A non-technical user can post a new article by following a simple, two-step process:\\\\n    1.  **Write the article:** Create a simple text file in Markdown format, with the filename `YYYY-MM-DD-your-title.md`.\\\\n    2.  **Upload the file:** Using the AWS Console, upload this single file to a specific S3 bucket (`hoa-news-uploads/incoming/`).\\\\n*   **Automation:** An AWS Lambda function will automatically trigger on upload, convert the Markdown to HTML, generate the new article page, update the `feed.json` file, and clear the CloudFront cache. The new article will appear on the public website within seconds.\\\\n\\\\n**Conclusion**\\\\n\\\\nThis comprehensive plan provides a complete, deterministic roadmap for developing the website's frontend. It directly addresses all user requirements for simplicity, security, and ease of use, with special attention paid to the non-technical content management process. My team and I are ready to proceed to the execution phase upon your approval.\\\",\\n  \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend-plan-01\\\"\\n}\\n###final-frontend-plan-report-01###\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":48615,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":4703,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":11252,\"outputTokens\":1049,\